 "note": "Rebased on 11_hoy.json (same scheme; Hoy's base livery was measured on Getty LAT 2201201240 and checked on Bellm's #12 Sutton 2175990645). Checked again on Sutton 2175990645 (Silverstone 1 April 1991, near side-on, left side): same Listerine nose, ESSO-headed number board, rising Securicor Omega Express block and Omega roundel; 'Bellm' in white letters on the rear side window. Wheels: white five-spoke from team-mate Hoy's Thruxton paddock photo (Getty LAT 2201200877); no standing photo of #12 found, Sutton 2175990645 shows the same light five-spoke wheels. Logos (2026-11-16): real logos for the BMW roundel on the sill, YOKOHAMA (white word, red Y mark) and the CHAMPION bow-tie; LISTERINE stays lettering because the saved Listerine wordmark is much narrower than the wide letters on the wing (crop of LAT 2201201240), and SECURICOR, OMEGA EXPRESS, the Omega roundel, NEO and STOPPERS have no logo file. NEO redrawn as yellow letters with a red outline over a red banner, and SECURICOR added on the front bumper face (both LAT 2201201240 / Sutton 2175990645). Round 1 look kept: from Thruxton (27 May) the car also carried a Shell pecten and Shell on the front apron instead of NEO, a Shell pecten with FUELS & LUBRICANTS at the top of the rear quarter and SPAX on the sill after Champion (LAT 2201201024, 2201222253, 2201200764); not drawn. Not drawn either: the STOPPERS box on the front lip and LISTERINE on the bonnet nose (medium confidence), the small white wordmark above NEO and the round emblem next to STOPPERS (not readable).",
